w22-write-precommit
-------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data or
weights; no code copied.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Zimo Xu, Wenzhuo Liu and Hideki Nakayama.
"CapLite: Prompt-Injection Defense for Small Language Model Agents without
Model-Written Security Artifacts". arXiv:2611.17115, v1, submitted 12 Nov
2026. Primary category cs.AI, cross-listed cs.CL and cs.CR.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17115
Licence: CC BY 4.0, http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ (the paper
licence shown on the abs page).

Code: the abs page links no code. None was found or used.

Method only: the rule that write calls are committed before any tool
result is read, and that a write is admitted only when every argument that
decides whom or what it affects is stated in the user's request, with the
policy derived from tool schemas rather than written by a model. The event
format, the substring and blank-value rules, the single-use commit, the
late-commit handling, the oracle and the fixtures are this sketch's own.
No text, figures, tables or data from the paper are copied into the code; the PDF was not read; no benchmark or model was run. The paper's claims
appear only in paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked UNVERIFIED.
